12. IF THEY ASK: WHY JdbcTemplate?
==================================================

Answer:

"For this requirement we already have a direct SQL query and we are retrieving only a defined set of fields. JdbcTemplate gives us a straightforward way to execute the supplied query using the existing Spring datasource and explicitly map the ResultSet, including the CLOB field."


==================================================
13. IF THEY ASK: WHY SPECIAL HANDLING FOR FINAL_QUERY?
==================================================

Answer:

"FINAL_QUERY can contain a large SQL statement and is stored as an Oracle CLOB. The helper method reads it through a character stream in chunks so the entire query can be returned without depending on a VARCHAR-size assumption."


==================================================
14. IF THEY ASK: WHY SERVICE CLASS?
==================================================

Answer:

"We keep the HTTP/controller logic separate from database logic. The controller only handles the REST request and response, while the service handles the database query and mapping."


==================================================
15. IF THEY ASK: WHY @JsonProperty?
==================================================

Answer:

"The Java variables follow camelCase naming, but the required JSON response needs the database-style field names such as FIELD_MAP_SK and TABLE_PHYSICAL_NAME. @JsonProperty controls those JSON field names."


